From 449322479bd2048789db473bafbc7ae5376c0bd8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Janne Grunau <j@jannau.net>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 19:23:15 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 36/37] pcie: Fix initialization on device with unused ports

Devices with unused ports like Mac minis (M1, M2, M2 Pro) or iMacs (M1
with 2 USB-C ports) skip over non-present "pci-bridge[0-3]" device node
but do not advance the `config_base` pointer to the next port. This
breaks the link speed configuration on Mac minis with 10 Gbps LAN.

Closes: https://github.com/AsahiLinux/m1n1/issues/756
Fixes: 77b0cdb7 ("pcie: Only initialize ports that are actually present")
Signed-off-by: Janne Grunau <j@jannau.net>

[j604: X4-02. The J604 apcie has pci-bridge0 (radio) and pci-bridge2
 (SD reader) but no pci-bridge1, so port 2's RC tunables, link speed
 and link width went to port 1's ECAM window; Linux saw root port
 00:02.0 at its 16 GT/s x2 reset defaults and the GL9755 trained at
 2.5 GT/s. For the m1n1 packager: 0036 on 1.607 (m1n1 1.608).]

Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Assisted-by: LLM
---
 src/pcie.c | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/pcie.c b/src/pcie.c
index 0478dd8a..5707038f 100644
--- a/src/pcie.c
+++ b/src/pcie.c
@@ -755,8 +755,11 @@ static int pcie_init_controller(int controller, const char *path)
                 break;
         }
 
-        if ((bridge_offset = adt_path_offset(adt, bridge)) < 0)
+        if ((bridge_offset = adt_path_offset(adt, bridge)) < 0) {
+            /* Move to the next PCIe device on this bus. */
+            config_base += (1 << 15);
             continue;
+        }
 
         printf("pcie: Initializing port %d\n", port);
 
-- 
